1
00:00:22,866 --> 00:00:24,868
♪ When the heat's coming down  

2
00:00:24,912 --> 00:00:27,088
♪ I keep it cool underground  

3
00:00:27,131 --> 00:00:28,567
♪ I get it in  

4
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:31,570
♪ I sweat it out  

5
00:00:31,614 --> 00:00:34,269
♪ On a roll, can't stop me now  

6
00:00:34,312 --> 00:00:35,879
♪ Got me falling off the ground... ♪  

7
00:00:52,113 --> 00:00:54,898
All right, Malia, stay in your lane!  

8
00:00:54,942 --> 00:00:57,901
Left wing, Julie! Left wing!  

9
00:00:57,945 --> 00:00:59,816
Come on, girls, hustle up!  

10
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:02,340
Good job, Warriors, good job!  

11
00:01:03,646 --> 00:01:07,128
Ladies and gentlemen, please clear the field.  

12
00:01:07,171 --> 00:01:08,781
I need everyone to move back to the parking lot.  

13
00:01:08,825 --> 00:01:10,783
Bring all your stuff with you.  

14
00:01:10,827 --> 00:01:13,177
Come on, move down to the parking lot.  

15
00:01:13,221 --> 00:01:14,700
Move back down to the parking lot.  

16
00:01:14,744 --> 00:01:15,745
Thank you.  

17
00:01:15,788 --> 00:01:16,920
All right, Warriors, bring it in,  

18
00:01:16,964 --> 00:01:18,139
bring it in.  

19
00:01:19,227 --> 00:01:21,925
Mom, I don't know anything about soccer.  

20
00:01:21,969 --> 00:01:23,709
They don't care. Just have fun, okay?  

21
00:01:23,753 --> 00:01:25,668
Go be with your team. I love you. Mmm.  

22
00:01:25,711 --> 00:01:27,148
Come on, get off the field, off the field.  

23
00:02:11,366 --> 00:02:13,368
Secure a perimeter and 24-hour security  

24
00:02:13,411 --> 00:02:16,937
while we recover all classified components, okay?  

25
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:18,547
Excuse me, Captain.  

26
00:02:18,590 --> 00:02:20,592
You can't move anything. This is a crime scene.  

27
00:02:20,984 --> 00:02:23,552
Jane Tennant, Special Agent in Charge, NCIS Hawai'i.  

28
00:02:23,595 --> 00:02:26,424
Well, Special Agent in Charge Tennant,  

29
00:02:26,468 --> 00:02:28,383
I'm Captain Joseph Milius.  

30
00:02:28,426 --> 00:02:30,428
Deputy Chief of Staff, Pac Fleet. I know.  

31
00:02:30,472 --> 00:02:33,431
Then I suspect you also know the protocol  

32
00:02:33,475 --> 00:02:35,520
for investigating an accident involving a Navy pilot.  

33
00:02:35,564 --> 00:02:38,262
Can we talk for a minute... privately?  

34
00:02:38,306 --> 00:02:40,047
Will it end this conversation sooner?  

35
00:02:40,090 --> 00:02:41,309
It's worth a shot.  

36
00:02:44,094 --> 00:02:46,270
Look, you can't be so sure this was an accident.  

37
00:02:46,314 --> 00:02:48,055
Because?  

38
00:02:48,098 --> 00:02:50,100
Because your pilot, Lieutenant Commander Walters,  

39
00:02:50,144 --> 00:02:52,102
reached out to my office 12 hours ago.  

40
00:02:52,146 --> 00:02:53,495
Wanted to file a report.  

41
00:02:53,538 --> 00:02:54,975
- About what? - Don't know.  

42
00:02:55,018 --> 00:02:56,977
Until I do, this is a crime scene.  

43
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:58,979
Well, call this site whatever you want,  

44
00:02:59,022 --> 00:03:00,371
but this is a top secret Navy program,  

45
00:03:00,415 --> 00:03:01,503
and I've got a job to do.  

46
00:03:01,546 --> 00:03:03,722
I know your next move, Captain.  

47
00:03:06,508 --> 00:03:08,379
Gonna run this up the chain of command?  

48
00:03:08,423 --> 00:03:10,686
But what's gonna come back down is that I'm in charge.  

49
00:03:10,729 --> 00:03:12,557
So all you're doing is delaying my investigation,  

50
00:03:12,601 --> 00:03:14,168
which isn't fair to Commander Walters,  

51
00:03:14,211 --> 00:03:16,126
his family...  

52
00:03:16,170 --> 00:03:18,172
or even you.  

53
00:03:23,655 --> 00:03:25,483
You should tell the wolf pack this was your idea.  

54
00:03:25,527 --> 00:03:27,485
It'll sell better.  

55
00:03:27,529 --> 00:03:29,183
Let's give it a beat, Tennant.  

56
00:03:30,749 --> 00:03:33,404
Make it more believable.  

57
00:03:36,451 --> 00:03:39,149
<i>Someone want to say how the fists started flying?</i>  

58
00:03:39,193 --> 00:03:42,196
- This punk wen touch my girl. - Just her nice necklace.  

59
00:03:42,239 --> 00:03:44,285
Okay, that's it-- you're coming in.  

60
00:03:44,328 --> 00:03:46,330
- Hey, those guys started it! - Keep it up and you'll go, too.  

61
00:03:46,374 --> 00:03:48,419
Officers, please, your tactics  

62
00:03:48,463 --> 00:03:51,422
are just really harshing my mellow.  

63
00:03:51,466 --> 00:03:53,598
How about you mind your own business, sir?  

64
00:03:53,642 --> 00:03:55,557
Look, um...  

65
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:58,516
Had a pretty simple situation here.  

66
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:01,171
These clowns disrespected the barkeep.  

67
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:03,043
My tattooed friend there tried to defend her honor.  

68
00:04:03,086 --> 00:04:04,044
And then, uh,  

69
00:04:04,087 --> 00:04:05,088
what do you do?  

70
00:04:05,132 --> 00:04:06,524
You separate them? No.  

71
00:04:06,568 --> 00:04:08,483
You have a thoughtful conversation  

72
00:04:08,526 --> 00:04:09,701
about the power of listening? No.  

73
00:04:09,745 --> 00:04:11,138
You kick ass, you take names,  

74
00:04:11,181 --> 00:04:12,617
and then you hope no one's filming.  

75
00:04:12,661 --> 00:04:14,706
Your I.D. Now.  

76
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:16,534
I haven't done anything wrong, so there's absolutely  

77
00:04:16,578 --> 00:04:18,188
no reason for me to share that with you.  

78
00:04:18,232 --> 00:04:19,581
All right, wise guy.  

79
00:04:19,624 --> 00:04:21,191
You're going in, too.  

80
00:04:21,235 --> 00:04:22,540
It's escalation.  

81
00:04:25,152 --> 00:04:26,544
Let's go.  

82
00:04:43,126 --> 00:04:45,563
- Morning. - Morning.  

83
00:04:50,742 --> 00:04:52,527
Ooh, pajama day?  

84
00:04:52,570 --> 00:04:53,745
I wish.  

85
00:04:53,789 --> 00:04:56,183
Youth soccer game at almost dark thirty.  

86
00:04:56,226 --> 00:04:57,445
I'm gonna need the rundown on our dead pilot  

87
00:04:57,488 --> 00:04:58,446
Lieutenant Commander Walters.  

88
00:04:58,489 --> 00:05:00,491
Background, fitreps...  

89
00:05:00,535 --> 00:05:02,798
Current assignment, friends and family, recent activity.  

90
00:05:02,841 --> 00:05:05,844
And dark Holualoa, splash of soy.  

91
00:05:05,888 --> 00:05:07,759
I have AFMES fast-tracking the autopsy.  

92
00:05:07,803 --> 00:05:09,413
Was there anything left to autopsy?  

93
00:05:09,457 --> 00:05:12,851
- Experimental F-35 - C had an emergency fail-safe.  

94
00:05:12,895 --> 00:05:15,376
Plane goes out of control, automatic ejection.  

95
00:05:15,419 --> 00:05:16,855
Although at that speed, the force of it  

96
00:05:16,899 --> 00:05:17,856
is probably what killed him.  

97
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:19,336
4-H weekend?  

98
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:21,686
No, cleaning campsites at Bellows Field.  

99
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:23,775
Here.  

100
00:05:23,819 --> 00:05:26,169
Jesse, it's my day, remember?  

101
00:05:26,213 --> 00:05:28,258
Oh, well, where's the new guy?  

102
00:05:28,302 --> 00:05:31,218
Not sure, but at some point, that will get old.  

103
00:05:31,261 --> 00:05:32,654
All right, guys, what else do we know?  

104
00:05:32,697 --> 00:05:35,222
Our pilot was at the stick of a top secret  

105
00:05:35,265 --> 00:05:37,789
experimental aircraft with self-flying capabilities.  

106
00:05:37,833 --> 00:05:39,443
He called last night, told the switchboard  

107
00:05:39,487 --> 00:05:41,184
he had something to report. Did he say what?  

108
00:05:41,228 --> 00:05:42,664
No. I left him a voice mail.  

109
00:05:42,707 --> 00:05:44,448
But he never returned.  

110
00:05:44,492 --> 00:05:46,276
Could be criminal activity, fraud,  

111
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:48,670
security leak, something personal.  

112
00:05:48,713 --> 00:05:50,541
And the crash could be completely unrelated.  

113
00:05:50,585 --> 00:05:52,152
All right, well, the program's on hold until we figure out  

114
00:05:52,195 --> 00:05:53,544
what happened, so that's gonna create some heat.  

115
00:05:53,588 --> 00:05:54,806
So, Lucy, I need you to go to AFMES  

116
00:05:54,850 --> 00:05:56,634
to get the autopsy results.  

117
00:05:56,678 --> 00:05:58,201
Jesse, I need you to... Hook up with Ernie.  

118
00:05:58,245 --> 00:06:00,377
Dive into Commander Walter's private life.  

119
00:06:00,421 --> 00:06:02,292
Please and thank you.  

120
00:06:05,904 --> 00:06:07,906
I got to handle something.  

121
00:06:14,217 --> 00:06:15,392
Mandarin?  

122
00:06:15,436 --> 00:06:18,308
Yeah. I want to read <i> Journey to the West</i>  

123
00:06:18,352 --> 00:06:19,918
in the original as Wu Cheng'en intended.  

124
00:06:19,962 --> 00:06:22,225
Hey.  

125
00:06:22,269 --> 00:06:24,401
I'm trying to get some insight into Lieutenant Commander...  

126
00:06:24,445 --> 00:06:26,490
Lieutenant Commander David Walters.  

127
00:06:26,534 --> 00:06:29,493
Graduated U.S. Naval Academy with distinction.  

128
00:06:29,537 --> 00:06:32,583
Multiple combat tours. Went Top Gun three years ago.  

129
00:06:32,627 --> 00:06:35,195
Transferred to the Pathfinders as a test pilot  

130
00:06:35,238 --> 00:06:36,631
- and instructor. - Ernie?  

131
00:06:36,674 --> 00:06:38,676
I'm looking for more color.  

132
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:42,419
Like why he was coming into NCIS before the kaboom?  

133
00:06:42,463 --> 00:06:44,378
Don't sweat it.  

134
00:06:44,421 --> 00:06:46,510
I'll just piggyback on his social media,  

135
00:06:46,554 --> 00:06:48,469
get a full sense of the man-- hopes, dreams,  

136
00:06:48,512 --> 00:06:50,471
weird fetishes if he had any.  

137
00:06:50,514 --> 00:06:53,213
I don't think Walters had social media, though.  

138
00:06:53,256 --> 00:06:54,953
Some fighter pilots don't.  

139
00:06:54,997 --> 00:06:57,260
Everyone else does.  

140
00:06:57,304 --> 00:06:59,523
His friends, family, dental hygienist.  

141
00:06:59,567 --> 00:07:01,525
He may not post,  

142
00:07:01,569 --> 00:07:03,223
but they certainly do.  

143
00:07:03,266 --> 00:07:04,963
I'm headed to the pilot's apartment-- call me.  

144
00:07:10,665 --> 00:07:12,536
How'd you know where I was?  

145
00:07:12,580 --> 00:07:14,886
Deputy sergeant texted me when he saw your credentials.  

146
00:07:14,930 --> 00:07:17,498
You know, I got over 50 résumés for your job.  

147
00:07:17,541 --> 00:07:19,326
Interviewed a dozen highly capable  

148
00:07:19,369 --> 00:07:20,892
candidates, including you.  

149
00:07:20,936 --> 00:07:22,416
Getting arrested two weeks in  

150
00:07:22,459 --> 00:07:23,982
makes me question my judgement.  

151
00:07:24,026 --> 00:07:26,985
Cops at the bar weren't being professional.  

152
00:07:27,029 --> 00:07:30,337
Local and vocal don't always jibe, and it was  

153
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:31,729
my obligation to correct their behavior.  

154
00:07:31,773 --> 00:07:33,253
No need to involve the badge.  

155
00:07:33,296 --> 00:07:35,124
Look, I won't pretend to know your experiences.  

156
00:07:35,167 --> 00:07:36,299
And I respect where you're coming from.  

157
00:07:36,343 --> 00:07:37,431
- Thank you. - Not done.  

158
00:07:37,474 --> 00:07:40,172
When anyone on my team gets in trouble,  

159
00:07:40,216 --> 00:07:41,652
I'm the first call.  

160
00:07:41,696 --> 00:07:43,698
Can't help if I don't know.  

161
00:07:43,741 --> 00:07:45,743
You can't live with that,  

162
00:07:45,787 --> 00:07:47,397
this isn't gonna work.  

163
00:07:49,094 --> 00:07:51,662
Understood. Won't happen again.  

164
00:07:55,579 --> 00:07:57,451
Hi. I'm gonna need  

165
00:07:57,494 --> 00:08:00,062
Commander Walters' preliminary results ASAP.  

166
00:08:00,105 --> 00:08:02,412
- Almost done. Gonna have to wait.  

167
00:08:02,456 --> 00:08:04,153
Whistler.  

168
00:08:04,196 --> 00:08:06,111
What's DIA doing here?"What are you doing here?"  

169
00:08:06,155 --> 00:08:07,374
is a more pertinent question.  

170
00:08:07,417 --> 00:08:09,550
Investigating a suspicious death.  

171
00:08:09,593 --> 00:08:11,682
Of a pilot who worked a top secret defense project?  

172
00:08:11,726 --> 00:08:14,250
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Silos, clearances, stakeholders.  

173
00:08:14,294 --> 00:08:16,252
Spare me. We've been read in.  

174
00:08:16,296 --> 00:08:18,080
No, and yet, Pac-Fleet asked  

175
00:08:18,123 --> 00:08:20,387
DIA to handle the dissemination of sensitive information,  

176
00:08:20,430 --> 00:08:22,563
so you will get the report when I clear it.  

177
00:08:22,606 --> 00:08:24,129
Thank you.  

178
00:08:33,878 --> 00:08:35,663
You're right.  

179
00:08:35,706 --> 00:08:37,534
- I know. - I shouldn't be so pushy.  

180
00:08:37,578 --> 00:08:39,797
- It's not a good look. - And I should respect the hierarchy.  

181
00:08:39,841 --> 00:08:42,278
Hmm, that'd be refreshing.  

182
00:08:42,322 --> 00:08:44,324
You still can't see it.  

183
00:08:48,850 --> 00:08:50,852
No, it's Inoki.  

184
00:08:50,895 --> 00:08:53,594
- Can you spell that? - I-N-O-K-I.  

185
00:08:53,637 --> 00:08:55,857
- K-I? Okay. - Yeah.  

186
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:58,250
- Give me an hour. - All right, I'll call back later, bye.  

187
00:08:58,294 --> 00:09:00,209
Hey, sorry.  

188
00:09:02,211 --> 00:09:04,561
- Got tied up. - Not to pile on, New Guy.  

189
00:09:04,605 --> 00:09:06,781
But I abandoned a conservation weekend to get here.  

190
00:09:06,824 --> 00:09:08,609
What's your excuse?  

191
00:09:08,652 --> 00:09:10,654
Got locked up by HPD.  

192
00:09:13,222 --> 00:09:14,876
Hey, it's been two weeks.  

193
00:09:14,919 --> 00:09:17,487
New Guy has a name.  

194
00:09:17,531 --> 00:09:20,185
Kai Holman. Born in Waimanalo.  

195
00:09:20,229 --> 00:09:22,449
Still holds the record for the most strikeouts  

196
00:09:22,492 --> 00:09:24,451
in the Interscholastic League.  

197
00:09:24,494 --> 00:09:26,844
Former Marine, including three years CID  

198
00:09:26,888 --> 00:09:28,846
before joining NCIS.  

199
00:09:28,890 --> 00:09:30,848
See, I listen. It's not bad.  

200
00:09:30,892 --> 00:09:32,546
And, uh, you are Jesse...  

201
00:09:32,589 --> 00:09:33,851
something with a B?  

202
00:09:40,641 --> 00:09:43,426
Don't see a lot of uniforms in places like these.  

203
00:09:43,470 --> 00:09:45,559
No photos, no bottles of booze.  

204
00:09:45,602 --> 00:09:47,430
TV's covered in dust.  

205
00:09:47,474 --> 00:09:49,345
Walters was a slave to his work.  

206
00:09:49,389 --> 00:09:52,566
But he's going to local places all over the island.  

207
00:09:52,609 --> 00:09:55,525
Anything suggest he had, like, a drug problem?  

208
00:09:56,744 --> 00:09:58,833
Nah, squad-mates say in the last few weeks  

209
00:09:58,876 --> 00:10:00,922
Walters was withdrawn and worn out.  

210
00:10:00,965 --> 00:10:03,185
But wasn't saying why.  

211
00:10:03,228 --> 00:10:04,969
Let's check the bedroom.  

212
00:10:10,584 --> 00:10:13,500
Commander Walters had a massive amount of dextroamphetamine  

213
00:10:13,543 --> 00:10:15,893
in his system-- 100 to 120 milligrams.  

214
00:10:15,937 --> 00:10:17,634
There were signs of toxic psychosis  

215
00:10:17,678 --> 00:10:19,462
and probable cardiac arrest.  

216
00:10:19,506 --> 00:10:21,421
Where's the autopsy report?  

217
00:10:21,464 --> 00:10:23,510
I didn't technically get it.  

218
00:10:23,553 --> 00:10:25,686
While Whistler read it, I read it upside down.  

219
00:10:27,470 --> 00:10:30,386
A trick I picked up during a summer congressional internship.  

220
00:10:30,430 --> 00:10:32,954
So we're looking at an overdose, intentional or otherwise.  

221
00:10:32,997 --> 00:10:36,305
All we found at his place was a bunch of supplements.  

222
00:10:36,348 --> 00:10:39,221
Though he's been hitting every dive bar on the island.  

223
00:10:39,264 --> 00:10:40,875
I only talked to Captain Milius for about ten minutes,  

224
00:10:40,918 --> 00:10:42,398
but he didn't seem like the type of guy  

225
00:10:42,442 --> 00:10:43,530
that would miss one of his pilots  

226
00:10:43,573 --> 00:10:44,705
having a drug addiction.  

227
00:10:44,748 --> 00:10:47,272
There are pursuits that compel a man  

228
00:10:47,316 --> 00:10:48,926
to retreat within himself.  

229
00:10:48,970 --> 00:10:50,885
In the East, it is often a sacred vow of silence.  

230
00:10:50,928 --> 00:10:51,929
In the West, a girl.  

231
00:10:51,973 --> 00:10:53,627
No sign of one at Walters'.  

232
00:10:53,670 --> 00:10:55,933
Maybe not, but back home in Grand Rapids,  

233
00:10:55,977 --> 00:10:57,718
they were abuzz.  

234
00:10:57,761 --> 00:10:59,633
Walters sent a photo to his sister who tagged it  

235
00:10:59,676 --> 00:11:01,635
for the rest of the family to see.  

236
00:11:01,678 --> 00:11:04,333
- Name's Noelani Ilihau. - Local.  

237
00:11:04,376 --> 00:11:05,900
Yep, and according to his little sister,  

238
00:11:05,943 --> 00:11:07,467
"she rocked his world."  

239
00:11:07,510 --> 00:11:10,339
Noelani's social media went dark a few weeks ago.  

240
00:11:10,382 --> 00:11:12,559
I tracked the plates  

241
00:11:12,602 --> 00:11:14,517
on the SUV in that photo.  

242
00:11:14,561 --> 00:11:17,781
1999 Pathfinder with expired registration.  

243
00:11:17,825 --> 00:11:20,567
The original owner cared enough to install LoJack.  

244
00:11:20,610 --> 00:11:22,743
Of course, the, uh, subscription lapsed.  

245
00:11:22,786 --> 00:11:24,484
You able to activate it?  

246
00:11:26,311 --> 00:11:27,922
Yes.  

247
00:11:32,492 --> 00:11:34,276
Turn back around again.  

248
00:11:34,319 --> 00:11:37,453
According to LoJack, we are literally on top of it.  

249
00:11:43,894 --> 00:11:45,330
What are you doing?  

250
00:11:45,374 --> 00:11:47,550
That Pathfinder's clearly off-road.  

251
00:11:47,594 --> 00:11:50,945
Some of these trails are about 150 years old.  

252
00:11:50,988 --> 00:11:52,773
So they're not gonna register on that tablet.  

253
00:11:52,816 --> 00:11:55,558
But...  

254
00:11:55,602 --> 00:11:57,473
they will on this.  

255
00:11:57,517 --> 00:11:59,344
OG GPS.  

256
00:11:59,388 --> 00:12:01,042
All right.  

257
00:12:01,085 --> 00:12:02,609
Here.  

258
00:12:02,652 --> 00:12:06,308
You're gonna need a hat and sunscreen.  

259
00:12:06,351 --> 00:12:08,353
Let's go.  

260
00:12:10,617 --> 00:12:12,793
That was a pretty fancy trick  

261
00:12:12,836 --> 00:12:14,969
you pulled taking a sneak peek at the autopsy.  

262
00:12:15,012 --> 00:12:17,624
Yeah, not sure Tennant thought so.  

263
00:12:17,667 --> 00:12:19,582
You worked for her a year now.  

264
00:12:19,626 --> 00:12:21,628
You know she doesn't hide where she stands.  

265
00:12:21,671 --> 00:12:24,500
Jim Carter worked for her longer.  

266
00:12:24,544 --> 00:12:26,415
And she fired him.  

267
00:12:26,458 --> 00:12:29,331
Jim Carter put himself over the team.  

268
00:12:29,374 --> 00:12:30,898
This is different.  

269
00:12:30,941 --> 00:12:32,769
You put the team over the mean girl.  

270
00:12:34,510 --> 00:12:35,990
Hey, it's fine.  

271
00:12:36,033 --> 00:12:37,948
I was here when Tennant took over, so she obviously  

272
00:12:37,992 --> 00:12:39,471
loves me best, but I'm pretty sure  

273
00:12:39,515 --> 00:12:40,951
you're her second favorite.  

274
00:12:42,474 --> 00:12:43,954
You really think Noelani  

275
00:12:43,998 --> 00:12:46,435
managed to get her SUV down this way?  

276
00:12:47,610 --> 00:12:48,916
I know she did.  

277
00:12:52,397 --> 00:12:54,008
Someone tried to dump it.  

278
00:12:54,051 --> 00:12:56,053
It...  

279
00:12:59,622 --> 00:13:00,580
And her.  

280
00:13:08,631 --> 00:13:12,592
M.E. thinks Noelani's been here for days. Neck's broken.  

281
00:13:12,635 --> 00:13:13,941
Car was in neutral, she's just laid out across  

282
00:13:13,984 --> 00:13:16,160
the driver's seat. Doesn't look like an accident.  

283
00:13:16,204 --> 00:13:18,119
Keep working the scene.  

284
00:13:18,162 --> 00:13:20,643
Hoping for an update?  

285
00:13:20,687 --> 00:13:22,602
Accident seems increasingly unlikely.  

286
00:13:23,777 --> 00:13:25,822
Giving you wide berth here out of respect for the position  

287
00:13:25,866 --> 00:13:28,042
you're in, but Walters' mother and sister  

288
00:13:28,085 --> 00:13:29,652
are flying in to take his remains.  

289
00:13:29,696 --> 00:13:31,785
You know that can't happen till this case is closed.  

290
00:13:31,828 --> 00:13:33,787
There is no case.  

291
00:13:33,830 --> 00:13:35,832
My people reviewed the mission computer.  

292
00:13:35,876 --> 00:13:37,747
Walters went into G-LOC, Crashed.  

293
00:13:37,791 --> 00:13:39,444
Commander Walters had dextroamphetamine  

294
00:13:39,488 --> 00:13:40,532
in his system.  

295
00:13:40,576 --> 00:13:42,099
It's in the tox screen.  

296
00:13:42,143 --> 00:13:44,058
And there are extenuating circumstances.  

297
00:13:44,101 --> 00:13:45,712
He was involved with a girl  

298
00:13:45,755 --> 00:13:47,017
whose body was dumped in the mountains.  

299
00:13:47,061 --> 00:13:49,019
You implying he killed her,  

300
00:13:49,063 --> 00:13:50,630
then killed himself in that plane?  

301
00:13:50,673 --> 00:13:51,631
I'm not implying anything.  

302
00:13:51,674 --> 00:13:53,807
Going where the case takes me.  

303
00:13:55,504 --> 00:13:57,898
Your jacket says top of your class at FLETC.  

304
00:13:57,941 --> 00:14:01,162
Only agent to receive the Medal of Merit three times.  

305
00:14:01,205 --> 00:14:04,121
But you know what people say?  

306
00:14:04,165 --> 00:14:06,123
You're stubborn  

307
00:14:06,167 --> 00:14:08,648
and incapable of staying in line.  

308
00:14:08,691 --> 00:14:10,650
And if I were you, they'd say I was  

309
00:14:10,693 --> 00:14:12,956
persistent and dedicated.  

310
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,958
Look, people are paying attention to this  

311
00:14:15,002 --> 00:14:16,656
all the way up the chain. One wrong move,  

312
00:14:16,699 --> 00:14:18,179
won't just be you and me taking the fall.  

313
00:14:18,222 --> 00:14:20,181
It'll be your team, too.  

314
00:14:50,646 --> 00:14:53,693
I'm making your favorite.  

315
00:14:53,736 --> 00:14:54,694
Medicine's in the bag, Dad.  

316
00:14:54,737 --> 00:14:56,391
- I got to split. - Go stay.  

317
00:14:56,434 --> 00:14:57,871
Eat this time.  

318
00:14:57,914 --> 00:14:59,394
That boss of yours, she's treating you like  

319
00:14:59,437 --> 00:15:01,526
- she the mastah or something. - No.  

320
00:15:01,570 --> 00:15:03,398
No, she's not bad.  

321
00:15:03,441 --> 00:15:05,922
Well, then she wouldn't mind you eating some saimin.  

322
00:15:07,663 --> 00:15:08,925
Here.  

323
00:15:08,969 --> 00:15:10,535
Look what I found.  

324
00:15:13,538 --> 00:15:15,453
Oh, and I ran into your friend.  

325
00:15:15,497 --> 00:15:16,977
The pretty wahine with the long hair.  

326
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:19,283
- Hina? - Yeah.  

327
00:15:19,327 --> 00:15:21,982
Come as a big surprise when I tell her you was home.  

328
00:15:22,025 --> 00:15:24,593
Hey, we should have a party.  

329
00:15:24,636 --> 00:15:27,291
And let everybody see you.  

330
00:15:27,335 --> 00:15:29,554
Be <i>'ohana</i> again.  

331
00:15:35,473 --> 00:15:37,388
Can't stay for dinner. I got work.  

332
00:15:37,432 --> 00:15:39,477
Hey, you sound like me in the <i>hanabaddah</i> days.  

333
00:15:39,521 --> 00:15:40,914
Yeah.  

334
00:15:40,957 --> 00:15:43,264
Except I'm here when <i>you</i> got sick.  

335
00:15:43,307 --> 00:15:44,613
She wouldn't want this.  

336
00:15:44,656 --> 00:15:46,746
It's a little too late for you to start caring  

337
00:15:46,789 --> 00:15:49,444
about what Mom wanted.  

338
00:15:49,487 --> 00:15:51,489
<i>M.E.'s initial report</i>  

339
00:15:51,533 --> 00:15:53,274
makes it pretty clear Noelani was dead  

340
00:15:53,317 --> 00:15:54,928
before she hit that ravine.  

341
00:15:54,971 --> 00:15:56,973
There was material under her fingernails.  

342
00:15:57,017 --> 00:15:58,975
We've expedited the DNA analysis.  

343
00:15:59,019 --> 00:16:01,456
Nothing in Walters' report points to him being violent.  

344
00:16:01,499 --> 00:16:03,371
I don't think he killed her.  

345
00:16:03,414 --> 00:16:05,286
Let's focus on Noelani, Figure out who she was.  

346
00:16:06,983 --> 00:16:08,376
Oh, crap.  

347
00:16:09,943 --> 00:16:11,292
I need a word.  

348
00:16:11,335 --> 00:16:13,468
Look, I can--Not with you. Her.  

349
00:16:18,429 --> 00:16:20,823
I brought Commander Walters' declassified incident report.  

350
00:16:20,867 --> 00:16:22,869
- Oh, terrific. - But I didn't need to.  

351
00:16:22,912 --> 00:16:25,785
Because I was informed by Captain Milius that NCIS  

352
00:16:25,828 --> 00:16:27,525
already saw the report. I told the captain  

353
00:16:27,569 --> 00:16:29,789
the report hasn't left my sight. That I take my work  

354
00:16:29,832 --> 00:16:31,791
and security protocols seriously.  

355
00:16:31,834 --> 00:16:33,793
And he wondered how that was possible,  

356
00:16:33,836 --> 00:16:35,403
since I failed so completely at both.  

357
00:16:35,446 --> 00:16:38,319
I am filing a complaint against your Special Agent.  

358
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:47,154
Look, if you have an issue, it's with me.  

359
00:16:47,197 --> 00:16:49,286
I'm the one who passed the information to Captain Milius.  

360
00:16:49,330 --> 00:16:52,246
Which you couldn't have done if she hadn't stolen it.  

361
00:16:52,289 --> 00:16:54,857
She just saw a few key phrases on a report that you're now  

362
00:16:54,901 --> 00:16:56,816
delivering to me. No harm, no foul.  

363
00:16:56,859 --> 00:16:59,383
No. Harm, foul.  

364
00:16:59,427 --> 00:17:01,037
I'm an intelligenceofficer.  

365
00:17:01,081 --> 00:17:02,909
My mission is to protect the intel.  

366
00:17:04,171 --> 00:17:06,086
And pissing off...  

367
00:17:06,129 --> 00:17:08,175
future admirals will not help my career.  

368
00:17:08,218 --> 00:17:10,307
Can I see the report, please?  

369
00:17:14,094 --> 00:17:16,748
And no need for a complaint. I'll clear it up with Milius.  

370
00:17:16,792 --> 00:17:20,187
With all due respect, he's more pissed at you than he is at me.  

371
00:17:21,536 --> 00:17:23,233
The lab analyzed the supplements  

372
00:17:23,277 --> 00:17:25,279
from Commander Walters' apartment. Yes.  

373
00:17:25,322 --> 00:17:27,411
Found high levels of dextroamphetamine.  

374
00:17:27,455 --> 00:17:29,936
They were spiked.  

375
00:17:29,979 --> 00:17:32,982
This crash just got a lot more complicated.  

376
00:17:35,463 --> 00:17:37,769
Hey, Alex, get me some lemongrass from outside.  

377
00:17:37,813 --> 00:17:39,249
Or get the door!  

378
00:17:39,293 --> 00:17:41,469
Hey, Mom, did I remain the right one?  

379
00:17:41,512 --> 00:17:44,080
Hang on, Jules.  

380
00:17:44,124 --> 00:17:45,342
Alex!  

381
00:17:46,387 --> 00:17:48,432
What?  

382
00:17:48,476 --> 00:17:50,478
Oh, the door was open.  

383
00:17:50,521 --> 00:17:52,132
Nothing.  

384
00:17:54,961 --> 00:17:56,223
Hey, Mr. Ernie.  

385
00:17:56,266 --> 00:17:58,312
Hey, Julie.  

386
00:18:00,270 --> 00:18:03,186
Jesse and Lucy found Noelani's phone at the crime scene.  

387
00:18:03,230 --> 00:18:05,362
Pulled the SIM card-- online profile  

388
00:18:05,406 --> 00:18:07,277
only goes back a few months.  

389
00:18:07,321 --> 00:18:09,279
Most of her friends on social media are bots.  

390
00:18:09,323 --> 00:18:11,455
Most of her pictures are photoshopped.  

391
00:18:11,499 --> 00:18:14,154
Anything actually real - about her? - Well, she really worked  

392
00:18:14,197 --> 00:18:16,939
as a cocktail waitress at a place called Namaka Ale House.  

393
00:18:16,983 --> 00:18:19,811
Paystubs go back a few weeks, then they abruptly stop.  

394
00:18:19,855 --> 00:18:21,813
Mmm, stew smells amazing.  

395
00:18:21,857 --> 00:18:23,380
Alex!  

396
00:18:23,424 --> 00:18:25,078
I need you to finish dinner and get your sister to bed.  

397
00:18:25,121 --> 00:18:27,080
- On time. - Why do I have to babysit?  

398
00:18:27,123 --> 00:18:28,559
It's not babysitting.  

399
00:18:28,603 --> 00:18:30,474
It's helping, Alex, and that's  

400
00:18:30,518 --> 00:18:33,129
what families do for each other.  

401
00:18:38,091 --> 00:18:40,006
I'd add lemongrass.  

402
00:18:40,049 --> 00:18:42,182
<i>Jane Tennant, NCIS.</i>  

403
00:18:42,225 --> 00:18:44,836
I'm looking for information on Noelani Ilihau.  

404
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,926
Not much to tell you.  

405
00:18:46,969 --> 00:18:49,319
She cocktailed for a while, one day didn't show.  

406
00:18:49,363 --> 00:18:51,104
That didn't worry you?  

407
00:18:51,147 --> 00:18:53,019
People come, people go.  

408
00:18:53,062 --> 00:18:54,934
That's the bar business.  

409
00:18:54,977 --> 00:18:56,936
Mind if I talk to the staff?  

410
00:18:58,894 --> 00:19:00,504
Look.  

411
00:19:00,548 --> 00:19:02,985
You're just doing your job, I get it.  

412
00:19:03,029 --> 00:19:05,988
But this is the <i>pau hana</i> crowd.  

413
00:19:06,032 --> 00:19:07,511
They want to relax.  

414
00:19:07,555 --> 00:19:09,905
Can't do that with cops around.  

415
00:19:09,949 --> 00:19:11,559
Please?  

416
00:19:14,431 --> 00:19:16,433
Another day, then.  

417
00:19:21,917 --> 00:19:23,571
<i>Hey, Kai. I was just about to call you.</i>  

418
00:19:23,614 --> 00:19:25,616
Yeah, I'm just, uh, at the office.  

419
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:28,097
Hey, those souvenirs from the places he visited,  

420
00:19:28,141 --> 00:19:30,230
there were dates on them, some after she died.  

421
00:19:30,273 --> 00:19:32,145
Walters was looking for her.  

422
00:19:32,188 --> 00:19:33,929
And if he got shut down at the bar she worked at,  

423
00:19:33,973 --> 00:19:35,887
like I just did, I'm guessing he didn't get far.  

424
00:19:35,931 --> 00:19:39,935
Uh, one of the souvenirs is from Ace's Surf Shop.  

425
00:19:39,979 --> 00:19:41,632
I know someone there. I'll check it out tomorrow.  

426
00:19:41,676 --> 00:19:43,417
Send me the address. I'll meet you.  

427
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:46,202
Look, I got to go alone.  

428
00:19:46,246 --> 00:19:49,118
You're new, so you haven't had the pleasure of my  

429
00:19:49,162 --> 00:19:50,641
"we work as a team" speech,  

430
00:19:50,685 --> 00:19:52,382
but you can guess the bullet points.  

431
00:19:52,426 --> 00:19:55,211
Allow me to impress you, okay?  

432
00:19:55,255 --> 00:19:57,431
And I will let you know what I know  

433
00:19:57,474 --> 00:19:59,563
as-as soon as I know it.  

434
00:19:59,607 --> 00:20:01,957
<i>Okay, I look forward to being impressed.</i>  

435
00:20:10,096 --> 00:20:13,012
Hey, Hina, I think you, uh,  

436
00:20:13,055 --> 00:20:15,623
missed a few spots there, yeah?  

437
00:20:19,192 --> 00:20:21,194
Look, I know it's been a while--  

438
00:20:25,633 --> 00:20:27,287
Welcome home, brah.  

439
00:20:36,557 --> 00:20:38,602
Here.  

440
00:20:38,646 --> 00:20:40,039
Where's da aloha?  

441
00:20:40,082 --> 00:20:41,910
I got to hear from your pops that you're back.  

442
00:20:41,953 --> 00:20:44,130
- I've been busy. - No, you've been hiding.  

443
00:20:48,221 --> 00:20:50,658
So why you come now?  

444
00:20:54,705 --> 00:20:56,577
Honestly...  

445
00:20:56,620 --> 00:20:58,013
work.  

446
00:21:01,930 --> 00:21:04,193
A pilot had this  

447
00:21:04,237 --> 00:21:06,630
at his house. And he died.  

448
00:21:06,674 --> 00:21:08,632
And then we just found his girlfriend yesterday murdered.  

449
00:21:08,676 --> 00:21:09,938
I don't know about no murders.  

450
00:21:09,981 --> 00:21:12,636
Yeah, but, look, maybe you...  

451
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:14,160
maybe you know her.  

452
00:21:14,203 --> 00:21:15,900
Name's Noelani.  

453
00:21:15,944 --> 00:21:17,554
That's not her name.  

454
00:21:17,598 --> 00:21:19,991
This is Allana.  

455
00:21:20,035 --> 00:21:23,169
We used to hang with her cuz from Nanakuli High.  

456
00:21:23,212 --> 00:21:25,649
She taught the wahine tourists how to drop  

457
00:21:25,693 --> 00:21:27,042
in on the two-footers  

458
00:21:27,086 --> 00:21:29,218
until someone offered her a new job a while back.  

459
00:21:29,262 --> 00:21:31,046
What kind of job?  

460
00:21:35,050 --> 00:21:37,531
Look, I'm here so that other cops won't be.  

461
00:21:37,574 --> 00:21:39,533
You can talk to me, okay?  

462
00:21:39,576 --> 00:21:40,882
We're <i>hoaaloha.</i>  

463
00:21:40,925 --> 00:21:43,145
Yeah, the same friend that joined the Marines  

464
00:21:43,189 --> 00:21:45,104
and left for the mainland.  

465
00:21:45,147 --> 00:21:46,714
Not even a "see ya."I had to leave, Hina.  

466
00:21:46,757 --> 00:21:48,150
I didn't want to talk about it.  

467
00:21:48,194 --> 00:21:49,499
And now, not even a "hey, I'm back."  

468
00:21:49,543 --> 00:21:50,631
I understand that you're mad at me.  

469
00:21:50,674 --> 00:21:52,850
Look, we all got our troubles, Kai.  

470
00:21:52,894 --> 00:21:54,635
Still...  

471
00:21:54,678 --> 00:21:56,550
you never turn your back on the ocean.  

472
00:22:01,163 --> 00:22:04,079
What about Allana's troubles?  

473
00:22:07,604 --> 00:22:09,650
Some buggah offered her a job.  

474
00:22:09,693 --> 00:22:11,782
Sort of like a hostess.  

475
00:22:11,826 --> 00:22:14,263
Get close to the guys.  

476
00:22:14,307 --> 00:22:16,613
Make them feel special. Paid good.  

477
00:22:16,657 --> 00:22:18,659
Sounded sketchy to me.  

478
00:22:18,702 --> 00:22:20,269
Who made the offer?  

479
00:22:20,313 --> 00:22:22,793
I don't know. Never saw him.  

480
00:22:22,837 --> 00:22:25,231
Had a funny kine nickname.  

481
00:22:27,102 --> 00:22:28,843
Big Luna.  

482
00:22:28,886 --> 00:22:32,194
Nothing in any law enforcement database  

483
00:22:32,238 --> 00:22:34,065
about a Big Luna-- either he knows how to stay hidden  

484
00:22:34,109 --> 00:22:35,806
or your source was playing you.  

485
00:22:35,850 --> 00:22:38,200
If my source says there's a Big Luna, there's a Big Luna.  

486
00:22:38,244 --> 00:22:40,724
All right, well, let's focus on Noelani or Allana.  

487
00:22:40,768 --> 00:22:42,683
What else do we know?  

488
00:22:44,119 --> 00:22:45,729
Don Sloane.  

489
00:22:45,773 --> 00:22:47,557
Dated our girl a few months last year.  

490
00:22:47,601 --> 00:22:49,646
She disappeared, he filed a missing persons report.  

491
00:22:49,690 --> 00:22:51,561
He's a DOD engineer?  

492
00:22:51,605 --> 00:22:53,650
- And works top secret aircraft. - Local girl  

493
00:22:53,694 --> 00:22:56,044
dates guys with need-to-know information, works them  

494
00:22:56,087 --> 00:22:58,264
until she becomes a ghost.  

495
00:22:58,307 --> 00:23:00,266
So at best we're dealing with a con woman. At worst...  

496
00:23:00,309 --> 00:23:02,877
- A spy. - So I'm guessing whoever's running the ring  

497
00:23:02,920 --> 00:23:05,009
killed Allana when Walters started looking for her.  

498
00:23:05,053 --> 00:23:06,750
Made sure that she couldn't be tied back to them  

499
00:23:06,794 --> 00:23:08,274
and then made sure Walters stayed quiet, too.  

500
00:23:08,317 --> 00:23:10,580
Well, me showing up at the Ale House is gonna spook them.  

501
00:23:10,624 --> 00:23:12,669
Where's Don Sloane now?  

502
00:23:14,323 --> 00:23:15,977
He's locked his location apps.  

503
00:23:16,020 --> 00:23:17,239
See if he has a fitness tracker.  

504
00:23:17,283 --> 00:23:19,328
Guys got busted using them on deployment.  

505
00:23:19,372 --> 00:23:20,764
Dudes take every precaution  

506
00:23:20,808 --> 00:23:22,157
until they want to log their miles.  

507
00:23:23,637 --> 00:23:25,291
Huh, he does.  

508
00:23:26,770 --> 00:23:29,295
Also got an anonymous IP logged into his account.  

509
00:23:29,338 --> 00:23:31,993
We're not the only ones tracking him.  

510
00:23:57,192 --> 00:23:58,280
You get his plates?  

511
00:24:00,717 --> 00:24:03,242
Damn.  

512
00:24:04,852 --> 00:24:06,854
All right, how about 6:00 tomorrow? Can I get Inoki then?  

513
00:24:09,160 --> 00:24:11,380
Yep, all right, I'll be there.  

514
00:24:11,424 --> 00:24:12,816
Hey.  

515
00:24:12,860 --> 00:24:14,253
- Everything okay? - Yeah, yeah.  

516
00:24:14,296 --> 00:24:15,993
How'd it go with Sloane?  

517
00:24:16,037 --> 00:24:17,995
Either he's a professional liar or he's telling the truth.  

518
00:24:18,039 --> 00:24:19,693
Which is...  

519
00:24:19,736 --> 00:24:21,042
Uber driver took him to the Namaka Ale House  

520
00:24:21,085 --> 00:24:22,304
where he met a waitress.  

521
00:24:22,348 --> 00:24:24,001
Allana.  

522
00:24:24,045 --> 00:24:26,177
They started to date, he thought it was the real deal,  

523
00:24:26,221 --> 00:24:28,310
which is why he reported her missing to HPD.  

524
00:24:28,354 --> 00:24:29,877
Yeah? Was he compromised?  

525
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:32,662
One night he blacks out, thought he had too much to drink.  

526
00:24:32,706 --> 00:24:35,317
Ended up at home, nothing out of place.  

527
00:24:35,361 --> 00:24:37,319
He didn't connect the dots until we did.  

528
00:24:37,363 --> 00:24:39,669
This is espionage.  

529
00:24:39,713 --> 00:24:42,237
What would you like today?  

530
00:24:42,281 --> 00:24:44,674
Hey, uh...  

531
00:24:44,718 --> 00:24:47,198
Kalua pig, uh... manapua.  

532
00:24:47,242 --> 00:24:49,723
And, uh, loco moco, yeah? Extra gravy!  

533
00:24:49,766 --> 00:24:50,941
- Shoots! - You want anything?  

534
00:24:50,985 --> 00:24:52,943
- Is that all for you? - No.  

535
00:24:52,987 --> 00:24:54,771
No, no, no, I-I've been here for, like, two weeks,  

536
00:24:54,815 --> 00:24:56,338
and I haven't paid for a single coffee.  

537
00:24:56,382 --> 00:24:59,210
So... thought I'd bring some culture to the team.  

538
00:24:59,254 --> 00:25:01,169
I'm pleading vegetarian on this one.  

539
00:25:01,212 --> 00:25:02,344
All right.  

540
00:25:02,388 --> 00:25:05,216
You're order number 15. Thanks, yeah?  

541
00:25:05,260 --> 00:25:07,349
All right.  

542
00:25:07,393 --> 00:25:09,873
You know, the things we do for our kids.  

543
00:25:09,917 --> 00:25:12,920
Hey, you're a good mom to give up the finer things in lunch.  

544
00:25:12,963 --> 00:25:15,357
My daughter would agree with you.  

545
00:25:15,401 --> 00:25:18,404
My son recently pretty much sees me as a prison warden.  

546
00:25:18,447 --> 00:25:20,319
Hey, it's hard being a mom.  

547
00:25:20,362 --> 00:25:22,495
It's, uh, it's hard being a son, too.  

548
00:25:24,932 --> 00:25:26,803
This whole case goes back to the bar.  

549
00:25:26,847 --> 00:25:29,066
Someone there is using locals to steal military secrets.  

550
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:30,981
And the only lead we have is a name.  

551
00:25:31,025 --> 00:25:32,418
Big Luna.  

552
00:25:32,461 --> 00:25:35,943
Ooh, looks like our spy ring didn't compromise Walters.  

553
00:25:35,986 --> 00:25:38,162
His credentials aren't being used  

554
00:25:38,206 --> 00:25:40,948
at anomalous IP addresses or multiple locations.  

555
00:25:40,991 --> 00:25:43,429
Yeah, well, they spoofed the hell out of Don Sloane's phone,  

556
00:25:43,472 --> 00:25:46,388
cracked his passwords, got specs  

557
00:25:46,432 --> 00:25:48,869
on the jet, code revisions, personnel lists.  

558
00:25:48,912 --> 00:25:50,784
Hoping there's something they didn't get.  

559
00:25:50,827 --> 00:25:52,438
Just what they needed from Walters,  

560
00:25:52,481 --> 00:25:54,744
which is info on the unmanned aerial capabilities.  

561
00:25:54,788 --> 00:25:56,224
Basically like a user manual.  

562
00:25:56,267 --> 00:25:58,400
Who on the personnel list would have access?  

563
00:25:58,444 --> 00:26:00,750
That's the irony. The spies know.  

564
00:26:00,794 --> 00:26:02,491
But we don't have access to that intel  

565
00:26:02,535 --> 00:26:04,972
unless DIA gives it to us.  

566
00:26:05,015 --> 00:26:06,756
So...  

567
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:08,454
time to practice our apologies.  

568
00:26:18,986 --> 00:26:21,075
Oh, look who's here.  

569
00:26:21,118 --> 00:26:23,120
Did you come by to clean up your mess  

570
00:26:23,164 --> 00:26:25,993
and save your ass? Or maybe take a swing at me?  

571
00:26:26,036 --> 00:26:28,212
No, no, no, I, um...  

572
00:26:28,256 --> 00:26:30,040
came to apologize.  

573
00:26:30,084 --> 00:26:32,869
I was out of line and put you in a jam.  

574
00:26:32,913 --> 00:26:34,828
And it wasn't right  

575
00:26:34,871 --> 00:26:37,134
or fair.  

576
00:26:37,178 --> 00:26:39,789
And I'm sorry.  

577
00:26:39,833 --> 00:26:43,314
♪ That I'm too young to know  

578
00:26:45,447 --> 00:26:49,451
♪ I love you so...  

579
00:26:49,495 --> 00:26:52,106
Oh, no, no, no, no, no. We-we can't do this again.  

580
00:26:52,149 --> 00:26:55,109
Uh, yeah, that's a horrible mistake.  

581
00:26:55,152 --> 00:26:57,807
Well, I wouldn't say horrible.  

582
00:26:57,851 --> 00:27:00,897
I'm agreeing with you.  

583
00:27:01,898 --> 00:27:06,207
♪ If we just wait a while  

584
00:27:06,250 --> 00:27:08,949
♪ No tears for us  

585
00:27:08,992 --> 00:27:11,342
No, that's okay. I'm not thirsty.  

586
00:27:11,386 --> 00:27:13,562
Why are you here?  

587
00:27:13,606 --> 00:27:15,564
♪ And wear a smile...  

588
00:27:15,608 --> 00:27:18,001
Commander Walters was murdered.  

589
00:27:18,045 --> 00:27:19,525
So was the girl he was seeing.  

590
00:27:19,568 --> 00:27:21,352
We think there's a spy ring stealing intel  

591
00:27:21,396 --> 00:27:24,921
on sixth-gen fighters. We can catch 'em with your help.  

592
00:27:24,965 --> 00:27:27,184
You want to know who else is working on the project.  

593
00:27:27,228 --> 00:27:28,490
I can get the info through channels, but you can  

594
00:27:28,534 --> 00:27:30,927
- get it faster. - What's in it for me?  

595
00:27:30,971 --> 00:27:33,277
Professionally speaking.  

596
00:27:33,321 --> 00:27:34,975
Uh...  

597
00:27:35,018 --> 00:27:37,020
do your job, stop the bad guys,  

598
00:27:37,064 --> 00:27:39,370
general sense of satisfaction.  

599
00:27:39,414 --> 00:27:41,068
Oh.  

600
00:27:44,245 --> 00:27:46,943
You know, I... I could use a drink.  

601
00:27:46,987 --> 00:27:48,597
Yeah, I think you should go.  

602
00:27:50,425 --> 00:27:53,036
And the list of names?  

603
00:27:55,561 --> 00:27:58,389
These are our most likely targets,  

604
00:27:58,433 --> 00:28:00,304
all DOD contractors and employees.  

605
00:28:00,348 --> 00:28:02,045
Whistler came through, but 20 names.  

606
00:28:02,089 --> 00:28:03,917
- Any way to narrow it down? - Sloane and Walters  

607
00:28:03,960 --> 00:28:05,875
were single, no dependents.  

608
00:28:05,919 --> 00:28:09,009
From the list, eight are married with families. Two others  

609
00:28:09,052 --> 00:28:10,532
started dating each other during the project.  

610
00:28:10,576 --> 00:28:12,882
- That leaves ten. - We need to find someone  

611
00:28:12,926 --> 00:28:14,405
with access to the same self-flying capabilities  

612
00:28:14,449 --> 00:28:16,538
as Commander Walters.  

613
00:28:16,582 --> 00:28:18,322
Charles Randolph.  

614
00:28:18,366 --> 00:28:20,324
Chief designer of the automated flying system.  

615
00:28:20,368 --> 00:28:22,109
Been at Pearl on and off for two years.  

616
00:28:22,152 --> 00:28:24,241
- Relationship status? - Separated.  

617
00:28:24,285 --> 00:28:26,896
Seems to have been kind of mopey until about two weeks ago.  

618
00:28:26,940 --> 00:28:29,551
- He met a girl. And according to an email he sent  

619
00:28:29,595 --> 00:28:31,379
from his work computer, her name is Sally.  

620
00:28:31,422 --> 00:28:32,641
Cocktail waitress.  

621
00:28:32,685 --> 00:28:35,078
- At the Namaka Ale House? - Yep.  

622
00:28:35,122 --> 00:28:36,950
And there's an anonymous IP address tracking  

623
00:28:36,993 --> 00:28:39,213
Randolph's phone, just like Don Sloane's.  

624
00:28:39,256 --> 00:28:40,910
They're going after him, too.  

625
00:28:40,954 --> 00:28:42,390
They didn't get what they wanted from Walters.  

626
00:28:42,433 --> 00:28:44,392
So they need this piece, or the rest of it's useless.  

627
00:28:53,053 --> 00:28:55,142
According to his cell phone, Randolph  

628
00:28:55,185 --> 00:28:57,274
arrived at the Ale House 15 minutes ago.  

629
00:28:58,449 --> 00:29:00,364
New Guy, you get in any trouble,  

630
00:29:00,408 --> 00:29:02,453
just say, "I'm new to the island," we'll come.  

631
00:29:08,459 --> 00:29:10,505
Got eyes on Randolph.  

632
00:29:12,376 --> 00:29:14,030
What you drinking?  

633
00:29:14,074 --> 00:29:16,337
Hey, uh, Hirata Shochu if you have it.  

634
00:29:16,380 --> 00:29:19,122
New batch coming - for the holidays. - All right, uh...  

635
00:29:19,166 --> 00:29:21,124
...green bottle, green bottle's fine.  

636
00:29:21,168 --> 00:29:22,473
Shochu?  

637
00:29:22,517 --> 00:29:24,563
It's a local spirit made with sweet potatoes.  

638
00:29:24,606 --> 00:29:26,565
Nectar of the gods.  

639
00:29:26,608 --> 00:29:29,350
Hey, Myra!  

640
00:29:31,004 --> 00:29:32,571
Any action in there, Kai?  

641
00:29:36,357 --> 00:29:38,272
It's all foreplay.  

642
00:29:38,315 --> 00:29:40,709
Bartender's serving Randolph off the menu, though.  

643
00:29:40,753 --> 00:29:43,103
They could be dosing him, like they did Don Sloane.  

644
00:29:43,146 --> 00:29:44,539
I got something else.  

645
00:29:44,583 --> 00:29:46,497
Dude at the bar hasn't touched his drink.  

646
00:29:46,541 --> 00:29:49,152
Busy watching Randolph - and the girl. "Dude?"  

647
00:29:49,196 --> 00:29:50,632
Got anything more to help?  

648
00:29:50,676 --> 00:29:52,373
Tattoo, parrot on the shoulder?  

649
00:29:52,416 --> 00:29:54,636
Signed affidavit he's Big Luna?  

650
00:29:54,680 --> 00:29:56,551
It's dead tonight,eh, bro?  

651
00:29:56,595 --> 00:29:58,597
Where's the party?  

652
00:29:58,640 --> 00:30:00,033
Hmm.  

653
00:30:00,076 --> 00:30:01,991
Everywhere's the same these days.  

654
00:30:02,035 --> 00:30:03,340
Yeah, yeah.  

655
00:30:03,384 --> 00:30:05,125
Man, there used to be a...  

656
00:30:05,168 --> 00:30:08,215
this, this-this joint, Helena's, you know?  

657
00:30:08,258 --> 00:30:10,086
It's barely a joint, it's just a shack.  

658
00:30:10,130 --> 00:30:11,697
They stay on School Street.  

659
00:30:11,740 --> 00:30:14,613
Yeah, yeah, that's right!  

660
00:30:32,195 --> 00:30:34,415
Hey, uh...  

661
00:30:34,458 --> 00:30:36,678
Which side of the road was Helena's on?  

662
00:30:36,722 --> 00:30:38,462
Was it...? North, bro.  

663
00:30:38,506 --> 00:30:40,682
Yeah, yeah.  

664
00:30:40,726 --> 00:30:43,206
Randolph's in play.  

665
00:30:43,250 --> 00:30:45,339
Being taken out back. Dude's not a local.  

666
00:30:45,382 --> 00:30:47,384
He's in on it.  

667
00:30:53,347 --> 00:30:55,218
Where you going, huh?  

668
00:30:55,262 --> 00:30:57,743
It's just, where, where's the bathroom in here?  

669
00:31:02,704 --> 00:31:04,793
Hey, I'm...  

670
00:31:04,837 --> 00:31:06,577
I'm new to the island... Jesse, Lucy!  

671
00:31:06,621 --> 00:31:08,405
You take the front, I got the back.  

672
00:31:30,123 --> 00:31:32,516
Federal agents!  

673
00:31:35,694 --> 00:31:38,392
Randolph's upstairs!  

674
00:31:41,525 --> 00:31:43,745
NCIS! Stop!  

675
00:31:43,789 --> 00:31:45,834
Hey! Let's go!  

676
00:31:50,796 --> 00:31:53,276
<i>How'd you know he wasn't local?</i>  

677
00:31:53,320 --> 00:31:55,670
I asked where Helena's was, he said north.  

678
00:31:55,714 --> 00:31:57,585
Real local would've said <i>mauka.</i>  

679
00:31:59,195 --> 00:32:00,719
Ernie, you got eyes on his vehicle?  

680
00:32:00,762 --> 00:32:02,633
Yeah, heading leeward at the fork.  

681
00:32:02,677 --> 00:32:05,724
- How far behind are we? - Let's just say go faster.  

682
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:11,120
Federal agents, keep your hands where I can see them!  

683
00:32:11,164 --> 00:32:12,339
Hey! Got her!  

684
00:32:24,220 --> 00:32:25,787
Damn!  

685
00:32:25,831 --> 00:32:27,920
Remind me never to piss you off, Lucy.  

686
00:32:29,356 --> 00:32:30,792
Suspect turned off-road  

687
00:32:30,836 --> 00:32:33,142
a quarter-mile ahead of your position, slowing down.  

688
00:32:33,186 --> 00:32:34,665
Guess he thinks he lost you.  

689
00:32:34,709 --> 00:32:36,189
Kind of feels like he did.  

690
00:32:46,547 --> 00:32:48,810
All right, daytime surveillance shows  

691
00:32:48,854 --> 00:32:50,551
a structure 100 feet from the coast.  

692
00:32:50,594 --> 00:32:52,596
Might be hard to see.  

693
00:32:54,250 --> 00:32:56,252
Not so hard.  

694
00:33:05,522 --> 00:33:07,524
NCIS!  

695
00:33:07,568 --> 00:33:08,961
Hands!  

696
00:33:38,904 --> 00:33:40,819
That's it!  

697
00:33:40,862 --> 00:33:42,821
You're out of road!  

698
00:33:44,561 --> 00:33:45,780
Put your hands up  

699
00:33:45,824 --> 00:33:48,261
and walk slowly towards me.  

700
00:33:53,527 --> 00:33:55,790
Hey! Hey, don't, don't, don't!  

701
00:33:59,968 --> 00:34:01,883
What the hell?!  

702
00:34:01,927 --> 00:34:04,625
No! No! No! No!  

703
00:34:07,323 --> 00:34:09,325
Really?!  

704
00:35:14,608 --> 00:35:16,915
Trust me!  

705
00:35:28,752 --> 00:35:30,972
Never turn your back on the ocean.  

706
00:35:31,016 --> 00:35:32,669
Noted.  

707
00:35:32,713 --> 00:35:34,845
Uh...  

708
00:35:34,889 --> 00:35:37,500
You kind of got us into this, you got a way to get us out?  

709
00:35:39,850 --> 00:35:41,983
Hey, hey!  

710
00:35:42,027 --> 00:35:43,767
The Coasties aren't lying.  

711
00:35:43,811 --> 00:35:45,639
They're always ready.  

712
00:35:55,040 --> 00:35:57,564
This everything we recovered from Big Luna's safe house?  

713
00:35:57,607 --> 00:36:00,480
Hard drives smashed. Files and photos burnt.  

714
00:36:00,523 --> 00:36:03,004
Just the kind of puzzle that gets my circulation going.  

715
00:36:03,048 --> 00:36:05,006
Did find this.  

716
00:36:05,050 --> 00:36:07,530
Dextroamphetamine. 100 milligrams per pill.  

717
00:36:07,574 --> 00:36:10,055
Colored to look like our pilot's vitamin supplements.  

718
00:36:10,098 --> 00:36:12,405
Big Luna must have snuck it into our pilot's house  

719
00:36:12,448 --> 00:36:13,754
- to dose him. - Mm-hmm.  

720
00:36:13,797 --> 00:36:14,929
DNA on his knife also matched what  

721
00:36:14,973 --> 00:36:16,409
was under Noelani's fingernails.  

722
00:36:16,452 --> 00:36:17,976
He killed her, too.  

723
00:36:18,019 --> 00:36:19,890
So we-we still don't know who he worked for  

724
00:36:19,934 --> 00:36:21,980
or how much of the jet program was compromised.  

725
00:36:22,023 --> 00:36:24,373
Hey, speak for yourself, New Guy.  

726
00:36:24,417 --> 00:36:26,549
Bartender Myra claims to be a victim,  

727
00:36:26,593 --> 00:36:29,030
but she served spiked drinks, led Randolph  

728
00:36:29,074 --> 00:36:31,554
up into the room, gave as good as she got  

729
00:36:31,598 --> 00:36:33,643
on the stairs with Lucy... Did not.  

730
00:36:33,687 --> 00:36:36,516
So I called a friend at Commerce and Consumer Affairs,  

731
00:36:36,559 --> 00:36:39,736
figured out who owns the bar, contacted their bank  

732
00:36:39,780 --> 00:36:41,086
about suspicious money transfers.  

733
00:36:44,045 --> 00:36:46,526
Did you time this - for when she walked in? - No.  

734
00:36:46,569 --> 00:36:48,528
That's just clean living.  

735
00:36:49,572 --> 00:36:51,400
That man forced me to help him.  

736
00:36:51,444 --> 00:36:53,098
Threatened my family!  

737
00:36:53,141 --> 00:36:55,622
- You saved me! - Compelling story, Myra.  

738
00:36:55,665 --> 00:36:57,624
Just not accurate.  

739
00:36:57,667 --> 00:36:59,408
The bar you work for is owned by a company  

740
00:36:59,452 --> 00:37:01,584
called the 'O Ahi Group. Hawaiian LLC.  

741
00:37:01,628 --> 00:37:03,978
Financed by a holding company based in Beijing.  

742
00:37:04,022 --> 00:37:05,806
Okay... It's a cover.  

743
00:37:05,849 --> 00:37:07,938
For the Chinese Ministry of State Security.  

744
00:37:07,982 --> 00:37:10,115
Our theory is you were born in Honolulu...  

745
00:37:10,158 --> 00:37:12,421
but trained by MSS.  

746
00:37:12,465 --> 00:37:14,075
I'd really think hard about what to say next.  

747
00:37:14,119 --> 00:37:15,772
Because my friend here...  

748
00:37:15,816 --> 00:37:17,818
hates spies.  

749
00:37:22,736 --> 00:37:25,043
Let's talk about experimental jets.  

750
00:37:35,488 --> 00:37:37,533
Ready... salute!  

751
00:37:49,980 --> 00:37:52,200
Something you need, Special Agent?  

752
00:37:54,507 --> 00:37:56,204
Lieutenant Commander Walters came to NCIS  

753
00:37:56,248 --> 00:37:58,511
because he suspected a spy ring.  

754
00:37:58,554 --> 00:38:00,121
Wouldn't have been able to stop it without him.  

755
00:38:00,165 --> 00:38:02,210
Wanted to pay my respects.  

756
00:38:06,519 --> 00:38:08,129
I'm known to be somewhat bullheaded.  

757
00:38:08,173 --> 00:38:09,870
"Somewhat"?  

758
00:38:09,913 --> 00:38:12,220
Okay... completely.  

759
00:38:12,264 --> 00:38:15,658
But if my attitude was... off-putting...  

760
00:38:15,702 --> 00:38:18,748
You said I was jeopardizing the careers of my entire team.  

761
00:38:18,792 --> 00:38:20,881
You wouldn't even take my call on Whistler's behalf.  

762
00:38:20,924 --> 00:38:22,970
I'm passionate about my people.  

763
00:38:23,013 --> 00:38:25,799
Tempers rise when you care.  

764
00:38:27,105 --> 00:38:29,150
Is this you apologizing?  

765
00:38:29,194 --> 00:38:31,152
Yes.  

766
00:38:32,197 --> 00:38:33,937
Well, it's very uncomfortable.  

767
00:38:36,070 --> 00:38:37,854
You did good work.  

768
00:38:37,898 --> 00:38:40,857
Stopped the bad guys, protected international security...  

769
